%I A398641 #10 Aug 11 2026 13:44:35
%S A398641 0,0,0,1,20,3749,1877694,1505997026
%N A398641 Number of connected quasi-quintic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398641 A quasi-quintic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 6 and all other vertices of degree 5. By the handshake lemma, such a graph necessarily has odd order.
%C A398641 The number of disconnected quasi-quintic graphs on 15 vertices is C_5(7)*R_5(8) + C_5(9)*R_5(6) = 1*3 + 20*1 = 23, where C_5(N) and R_5(N) denote the connected quasi-quintic and 5-regular graph counts on N vertices, respectively.
%H A398641 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ConnectedGraph.html">Connected Graph</a>.
%H A398641 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-QuinticGraph.html">Quasi-Quintic Graph</a>.
%e A398641 a(7) = 1505997026 because 23 of the 1505997049 quasi-quintic graphs on 15 vertices are disconnected.
%Y A398641 Cf. A398638 (quasi-cubic graphs).
%Y A398641 Cf. A398639 (connected quasi-cubic graphs).
%Y A398641 Cf. A398640 (not-necessarily-connected quasi-quintic graphs).
